# What EAS uploads when it builds the app.
#
# EAS archives from the repository root, not from frontend/, so the paths here
# are repo-relative. When this file exists it replaces .gitignore for the
# archive, which means every exclusion the upload needs has to be restated
# here — including the ones that keep secrets out.
#
# The one thing this file exists to *add* is the engine:
# frontend/modules/rpsfish/ios/RPSFish.xcframework and
# frontend/modules/rpsfish/android/libs, which .gitignore excludes because they
# are build artifacts of the engine's own repository. The EAS builder cannot
# produce them — the engine is Rust, in a separate repository — so they have to
# travel with the upload. They are included here by simply having no rule;
# `npm run build:rpsfish:ios` and `build:rpsfish:android` refresh them, and a
# stale library is a stale engine with no sign that anything is wrong.
#
# frontend/google-services.json, Firebase's config for Android match alerts,
# travels the same way: gitignored because the repository is public, and
# included here by having no rule. Without it the Android build has no alerts.
#
# Two things about EAS's matcher, both found by inspecting the archive rather
# than from the docs. A directory needs both its bare name and a `dir/**`
# glob: a plain `dir/` with a trailing slash matches nothing and the whole
# tree ships. And a negated directory glob wins over everything after it, so
# the `/*` + `!/frontend/**` allow-list shape cannot work here — it re-includes
# frontend's build output with no later rule able to take it back out. (The
# docs' `!` example is a single file placed last, which is a narrower thing.)
# Verify any change to this file by reading the archive it produces:
#   eas build:inspect --platform ios --stage archive --output /tmp/archive

# Not part of an app build.
backend
backend/**
deploy
deploy/**
docs
docs/**
tools
tools/**
.github
.github/**
*.md
.DS_Store

# Secrets, restated from the .gitignore this file replaces. deploy/ above
# already covers the bot tokens and deploy.env; these cover a stray anywhere.
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.jks
*.pem
*.mobileprovision
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
frontend/.env.development
frontend/.env*.local

# .env.production is deliberately not excluded: it is tracked, and the
# production bundle needs the EXPO_PUBLIC_ values in it.

# Installed on the builder from package-lock.json.
frontend/node_modules
frontend/node_modules/**

# Generated on the builder by `expo prebuild`. The local copies are stale and
# carry absolute paths from wherever this checkout used to live, so uploading
# them would quietly build the wrong thing instead of failing.
frontend/ios
frontend/ios/**
frontend/android
frontend/android/**
frontend/modules/rpsfish/android/build
frontend/modules/rpsfish/android/build/**
frontend/modules/rpsfish/android/.cxx
frontend/modules/rpsfish/android/.cxx/**

# Local build output and caches.
frontend/.expo
frontend/.expo/**
frontend/dist
frontend/dist/**
frontend/web-build
frontend/web-build/**
frontend/expo-env.d.ts
frontend/.idea
frontend/.idea/**
frontend/.kotlin
frontend/.kotlin/**
frontend/*.tsbuildinfo
frontend/.metro-health-check*

# Web-only engine artifacts. A native build loads the XCFramework instead.
frontend/public/rpsfish/*.wasm
frontend/public/rpsfish/rpsfish-worker.js
